<head>
  <title>Indexs: Program for computing vegetation index and other indices of interest in remote sensing</title>
<meta content="text/html; charset=ISO-8859-1" http-equiv="Content-Type"/></head>

<body>
  <!--Aquí inicia la part corresponent al titol de la MSA. Aquesta part s'ha d'editar desde el document WPS (aplicacio.mps).-->
<h1><span id="wpstitol"/></h1>
<!--Aquí acaba la part corresponent titol de la MSA editable de el WPS.-->
  <p>This program allows to easily calculate vegetation
  indices and other indices of interest in remote sensing from a predefined set. In case the index of interested is not available in this program, it can be calculated through the <a href="CalcIMG.htm">CalcImg</a> application. It is also posible to use <a href="CalcIMG.htm">CalcImg</a> application to rescale the output values.</p>

  <p>Vegetation indexes are spectral band combinations that enhance the contribution of certain observed components (typically vegetation) in the spectral response of a surface, minimizing other effects such as soil, illumination and atmosphere conditions, that can cause interference in the radiometric signal.</p>

  <p>The use of quotients and indexes to discriminate vegetation is based on
  the peculiar radiometric behavior of vegetation. The advantage of indexes
  in front the use of single spectral bands is that it shows a better
  correlation with ecological and agronomic parameters such as biomass, leaf
  area index (LAI), etc.</p>

 <p>This program currently has the following indexes implemented. Note: in the formulas <i>V</i> corresponds to the green (G) band, <i>IRp</i> corresponds to the near infrared (NIR) band and <i>IRoc</i> corresponds to the short wave infrared (SWIR).<br/>
  <br/></p>

   <!--Aquí inicia la part corresponent a les opcions de de la MSA. Aquesta part s'ha d'editar desde el document WPS (aplicacio.mps).-->
<span id="wpsopcions"/><br/>
<!--Aquí acaba la part corresponent a les opcions de de la MSA editable de el WPS.--> 

  <p>The program asks for the names of the files corresponding to the red,
  infrared and blue bands (only atmospheric indexes). It also requires a set
  of parametres that depend on the index equation. If they are not given in
  the command line, the program will ask for them interactively, suggesting a
  possible value (for example <img alt="gamma" src="gamma.gif"/>=1.06,
  <img alt="delta" src="delta.gif"/>=2.55, L=0.5).</p>

  <p>The NoData values of the original files are stored as NoData values in the
  output file. Negative square roots and zero deviding factors are also stored
  as NoData values.</p>

  <p>This application supports all MiraMon raster formats, as input, whether
  compressed or not, and generates a &quot;real-RLE&quot; type raster when all
  the input files are compressed in RLE format, and of the &quot;real&quot;
  type in all other cases.</p>
  
  <p><b><u>Additional references:</u></b></p>
<p><b>Pons X, Arcalís A</b> (2012) <i>Diccionari terminològic de teledetecció</i> Enciclopèdia Catalana i Institut Cartogràfic de Catalunya, Barcelona. 597 p. ISBN: 978-84-412-2249-6. <a href="https://www.termcat.cat/ca/Diccionaris_En_Linia/197">https://www.termcat.cat/ca/Diccionaris_En_Linia/197</a>.</p>

  
